<ProjectTemplate
  title="Stock Data Generator"
  link="https://github.com/michaelzhan1/stock-data-generator"
>
  <p>
    This was inspired by an interview question from a friend's team: given a
    stream of stock data, design a system to query the max price in a recent
    time range. I thought it would be fun to build a simple version of this out
    and visualize it. The stock data is simulated with geometric brownian motion
    in a Go backend and is served to the frontend through SSE. The frontend
    handles a min and max calculation using the sliding window max approach and
    displays real-time data with the <a
      href="https://github.com/ChartGPU/ChartGPU"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">ChartGPU</a
    > library.
  </p>
</ProjectTemplate>
